subproblems.statement:
Let P, Q, n ∈ ℕ. Let U, Z, M ⊆ ℝ^P, θ : ℝ^P → ℝ and ξ : ℝ^P → Λ_n(ℝ^P) satisfy IsRectifiableTriple U n M θ ξ. Let f : ℝ^P → ℝ^Q and L : ℝ^P → L(ℝ^P, ℝ^Q) be arbitrary maps and K ⊆ ℝ^Q any set. Assume:
- Z ⊆ U;
- Hⁿ(M ∖ Z) = 0, where Hⁿ = μHE[n];
- K′ := f⁻¹(K) ∩ Z is compact;
- there is C ∈ ℝ with ‖L(x)‖ ≤ C for all x ∈ M ∩ K′.
Then there is an Hⁿ⌞M-integrable h : ℝ^P → ℝ with ‖θ(x)·L(x)_#ξ(x)‖ ≤ h(x) for Hⁿ⌞M-a.e. x such that f(x) ∈ K.
